It would be more precise to write $F(\mathcal{A}) \otimes _\mathcal {O}^\mathbf {L} F(\mathcal{A}) \to F(\mathcal{A} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{A}) \to F(\mathcal{A})$ were $F$ denotes the forgetful functor to complexes of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. Also, note that $\mathcal{A} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{A}$ indicates the tensor product of Section <a href="/tag/0FRM" data-tag="0FRM">24.15</a> so that $F(\mathcal{A} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{A}) = \text{Tot}(F(\mathcal{A}) \otimes _\mathcal {O} F(\mathcal{A}))$. The first arrow of the sequence is the canonical map from the derived tensor product of two complexes of $\mathcal{O}$-modules to the usual tensor product of complexes of $\mathcal{O}$-modules.